'' =====================================================================
'' conflict-testO-scopexy-parser-hang.spin2  --  settles H-5
''
'' *** RUN THIS ONE LAST, ON ITS OWN. IT MAY HANG PNut. ***
'' *** Do NOT run it in the same session as K/L/M/N -- if it hangs, anything ***
'' *** queued behind it never executes and you lose those captures.          ***
''
'' QUESTION: does a BARE NUMBER in a SCOPE_XY *create* message hang the parser?
''   SCOPE_XY_Configure's loop is
''       while not NextEnd do begin  if NextKey then ... else if NextStr then ...  end
''   An `ele_num` element matches NEITHER branch, so `ptr` is never advanced and
''   NextEnd never fires -> a suspected INFINITE LOOP.  (Contrast SCOPE, whose loop
''   is `while NextKey do` -- a stray number merely TRUNCATES the parse there, and
''   contrast FFT, which is `while NextKey do` too and is therefore NOT exposed.)
''
'' This was derived from source by the REF team and has NEVER been observed.  It is
'' the one finding in this sweep we refuse to write into the manual unverified: an
'' unconfirmed hang claim is worse than silence.
''
'' TWO-RAIL DESIGN (order matters -- the safe rail runs and SAVES first):
''   RAIL-GOOD (known-true, runs first): a well-formed SCOPE_XY create -- every
''     number follows the keyword that consumes it, the label string comes last.
''     It must appear and SAVE.  That proves SCOPE_XY works in this session, so a
''     later failure cannot be blamed on the window type.
''   REAL CASE (runs last): `SCOPE_XY Bad 128 'A'` -- the 128 follows NO keyword.
''
'' OUTCOME -- there is no bitmap for the real case; the evidence is behavioural:
''   HANG      : PNut stops responding; the 'Bad' window never appears; the
''               "still alive" TERM counter below STOPS advancing.  -> CONFIRMED.
''               Kill PNut.  This becomes a documented footgun in ch08.
''   NO HANG   : the counter keeps advancing and/or a 'Bad' window appears.
''               -> REFUTED (or the window merely truncates, like SCOPE).  Say which.
''
'' The TERM heartbeat is the instrument: it is what distinguishes "PNut hung" from
'' "the window just didn't open".  Watch it, not the SCOPE_XY window.
'' =====================================================================

CON
  _clkfreq = 100_000_000

PUB main() | i

  ' Heartbeat -- this is how we tell a HANG from a merely-absent window
  debug(`TERM Beat SIZE 30 3 TEXTSIZE 14)
  debug(`Beat 'alive: ')

  ' ---- RAIL-GOOD: a well-formed SCOPE_XY. Must appear, must save. ----
  debug(`SCOPE_XY Good SIZE 150 RANGE 100 SAMPLES 0 DOTSIZE 6 BACKCOLOR BLACK 'A')
  repeat i from 0 to 3
    debug(`Good `(i * 40 - 60) `(0))
  waitms(300)
  debug(`Good save 'hangO_good')          ' filename LAST, nothing after
  waitms(300)

  ' prove we are still running BEFORE the dangerous line
  repeat i from 1 to 5
    debug(`Beat 13 'pre  ' `udec_(i))
    waitms(200)

  ' ================= THE REAL CASE -- may never return =================
  ' `128' follows no keyword.  If the parser hangs, everything below this line
  ' never runs and the heartbeat freezes at "pre 5".
  debug(`SCOPE_XY Bad 128 'A')
  ' ====================================================================

  ' If we get here, the parser did NOT hang.  The heartbeat resumes counting.
  repeat i from 1 to 20
    debug(`Beat 13 'post ' `udec_(i))
    waitms(200)

  debug(`Beat 13 'NO HANG - parser recovered')

  ' ---- LOG-FREE EVIDENCE CHANNEL (added 2026-07-14, for the PNut re-run) ----
  ' PNut emits no debug log, so the heartbeat above is invisible to read-back.
  ' Make the FILE ITSELF the evidence: this SAVE is only reachable if the parser
  ' survived the line above.
  '     hangO_survived.bmp EXISTS  -> NO HANG   (parser recovered)
  '     hangO_survived.bmp MISSING -> HANG      (execution never got here)
  ' hangO_good.bmp is saved BEFORE the dangerous line, so it exists either way --
  ' its presence proves the program ran and SAVE works in this session, which is
  ' what makes the ABSENCE of hangO_survived.bmp meaningful rather than ambiguous.
  waitms(300)
  debug(`Beat save 'hangO_survived')

  waitms(500)
  repeat
